The Bible Answers Vital Questions of Our Day
IS THE Bible relevant today?
For the answer to be yes, surely this age - old book would have to offer its readers guidance on topics of current interest and relevance.
Let us take a look at two current issues. In doing so, we will examine what the Bible says about these matters.
Why Does God Allow Suffering?
In view of the conditions in the world today, one of the most commonly asked questions is: Why does God allow innocent people to suffer?
This question is justified, since more and more people are being affected by violent crime, corruption, genocide, personal tragedy, and so forth.
When Jehovah God created the earth and everything on it, he did not intend that humankind be troubled by wickedness and suffering.
Of course not!
In the same way, when God pronounced everything “very good, ” there was no trace of wickedness on earth. So when and how did wickedness start?
He allowed for the passing of time so that it would become evident that humans cannot successfully direct their steps independent of him.
But has it not been better to wait until every conceivable doubt about the rightness of Jehovah’s sovereignty and the integrity of humans to him is dispelled?
Is it not true of present judicial systems that a court case to prove who is right and who is wrong may take years? In view of the importance of the issues facing Jehovah and mankind — universal sovereignty and the integrity of humans — how wise it was of God to allow for time to pass!
Now we see clearly what happens when humans ignore God’s laws and take charge of their own affairs. The result is widespread evil.
On the other hand, those faithful to God can look forward to a time, now near at hand, when “death will be no more, neither will mourning nor outcry nor pain be anymore. ” — Revelation 21: 4.
What Is the Purpose of Life?
Perhaps now more than at any other time in mankind’s history, people are trying to find out what life is all about.
Many ask themselves, ‘ Why am I living? How can I find meaning in my life? ’
Other individuals build their lives around a career, but they discover that power, prestige, and possessions fail to satisfy the inner yearning to find a reason for their existence.
Did the rebellion of Adam and Eve cause Jehovah to change his purpose?
Well, consider this point: The Bible was written thousands of years after the rebellion in Eden.
The obvious conclusion is that his purpose for the earth and mankind remains unchanged.
What God Expects of Us
Clearly, then, we can have confidence in the fulfillment of God’s purpose to have the earth inhabited forever by obedient humans. If we are to be among those privileged to live permanently on earth, we must do what wise King Solomon said: “Fear the true God and keep his commandments.
Once you discover the true value of its guidelines for life, you may well feel as did the psalmist who looked to Jehovah God for guidance and sang: “Your word is a lamp to my foot, and a light to my roadway. ” — Psalm 119: 105.
