It would be wrong to conclude, however, that distrust of authority characterizes only the younger generation. Today, people of all ages view any kind of authority with distrust, even contempt.
If exercised properly, authority, defined as “the power or right to control, judge, or prohibit the actions of others, ” can be a force for good. It can be of benefit both to individuals and to the community.
Respect for Authority — Why Essential?
WHO is not grateful that the police have the authority to arrest criminals who steal our possessions or threaten our family?
